{:id "0051-lab-board"
 :title "Lab board: a few pads that mark what you just wrote, and one XY pad for your style (no parameters)"
 :lupa/deps #{"0052-lab-dress"}
 :lupa/area :lab
 :lupa/risk :medium
 :goal "docs/product/score.md, 'How people and agents drive it'. People
        will not tune parameters. Give them an instrument instead: a small
        board, hidden until asked for, with pads that say what the last
        phrase is doing (STRESS, HOLD, ASIDE, TURN, DOUBT, LAND), one big
        moment (BOOM, a card), and one XY pad whose position is the
        writer's style: energy across, flourish up. Keyboard first. The
        Cramer end of the dial."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/lab/board.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/board_test.cljc"
         "src/halfahead/lab/pose.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/pose_test.cljc"
         "src/halfahead/lab/main.cljs" "src/halfahead/lab/debug.cljc"
         "test/halfahead/lab/debug_test.cljc" "public/lab/index.html"
         "e2e/lab.mjs" "docs/LAB.md"]
 :design "Schema (the foreman's; do not edit): :ha/style-point,
          :ha/mark-kind, :ha/word-cue's :source :board, :ha/direction.
          halfahead.lab.board (.cljc, pure):
          pads -> the board's pads in order, data: [{:id :stress :label
            \"STRESS\" :key \"1\"} {:id :hold ..\"2\"} {:id :aside ..\"3\"}
            {:id :turn ..\"4\"} {:id :doubt ..\"5\"} {:id :land ..\"6\"}
            {:id :boom :label \"BOOM\" :key \"7\"}].
          (target text selection) -> the [from to) span a pad acts on, in
            UTF-16 units, or nil when there is nothing to mark: the
            selection {:from :to} when it is not empty (trimmed of
            whitespace at both ends); else the last phrase: from the end
            of the previous sentence (after . ! ? … or a newline, and any
            spaces) to the end of the text without trailing whitespace,
            and no more than its last 12 words.
          (press pad point glyphs span t amount) -> what a pad adds to the
            draft at time t, {:cues [...]} or {:directions [...]}: a mark
            pad places one :ha/placed-cue on the glyphs in the span (as
            lab.reading maps spans to glyphs) whose cue is (marks/
            gesture-for point {:kind pad :amount amount ...}), forced to
            perform even in a spare style (a pad is a deliberate act: if
            gesture-for gives nil, use the gesture it would choose at
            flourish 1), with :source :board and :word the span's text
            (at most 64 chars); BOOM places a :ha/direction {:shot :card
            :energy amount :source :rules} on those glyphs. amount is 0.7
            for a tap and rises to 1.0 for a pad held 600 ms or longer.
          (xy->point point x y) -> point with :energy x and :flourish y
            (both kept in [0 1]); (point->xy point) -> [x y].
          lab.pose: frame's :style-choice may also be a :ha/style-point;
            then births and cues use (style/from-point point) and the
            frame has no :style key. Everything else as before.
          lab.main and index.html: a 'Board' toggle in the bar and Ctrl+B
            show and hide the board (hidden on load; remembered per viewer
            in localStorage, every access in try/catch). The board is
            real buttons in a toolbar labelled 'Board', each with its
            name and key, operable by Tab and Enter/Space, and by Alt+1 to
            Alt+7 from the textarea without it losing focus or gaining a
            character. Pressing a pad calls board/press on the board's
            target with the style point in force, adds the result to the
            draft (cues, or directions, exactly as typing would have) and
            voices it when sound is on. A pad with nothing to mark does
            nothing. Board cues survive like any cue: an edit that removes
            their glyphs removes them.
            The XY pad is a square with a dot: dragging or clicking sets
            the point, arrow keys move it by 0.05 when it has the focus,
            and it has an accessible name and value text ('Energy 60%,
            flourish 40%'). Moving it makes the style 'Mine': the style
            picker gains a Mine option that is selected then, and picking
            a named style moves the dot to that style's point (style/
            point). The point is remembered per viewer. With Mine picked,
            frame gets the point as :style-choice.
            window.__lab.board() -> {visible point target} as plain data.
            The debug overlay shows 'style mine (e 0.60 f 0.40 s 0.50 w
            0.50)' when a point is in force, and board cues read like any
            other ('did it -> glow 0.7 (board)').
          Tests: target for a selection, for text ending mid-sentence,
          after a full stop, with trailing spaces, over 12 words, empty;
          press for each mark pad at Plain's and Caffeinated's points
          (the forced gesture in a spare style), the amount from the hold,
          BOOM's direction; xy round trip; pose with a point as
          :style-choice equals pose with params from from-point, and
          every existing pose test passes unchanged.
          e2e/lab.mjs, a new step 'board' (?debug&reveal=3, Plain): the
          board is hidden on load; Ctrl+B shows it; type 'we did it'; click
          STRESS: the overlay shows a (board) cue on 'we did it' and a
          sampled frame shows those letters moving; Alt+2: a swell on the
          same phrase, and the textarea still has the focus and the same
          text; select 'did' and press LAND: the cue's glyphs are those of
          'did' only; BOOM places a :card direction (window.__lab
          .directions()); click the XY pad's top right corner: board()
          .point has energy and flourish above 0.9, the picker shows Mine,
          and the next cue's gesture plays faster than the same one in
          Plain (compare the time from its start to rest in sampled
          frames, by data not by clock); reload: the board is still
          shown and the point kept. Screenshot out/lab/board.png."
 :acceptance
 ["board, pose and debug tests as in the design, on both hosts"
  "`bb lab:e2e` passes with the board step and every existing step; `bb
   test` stays green; out/lab/board.png for the foreman"]
 :non-goals
 ["No learning from choices (the flick is a later order); no dress"
  "No change to marks, gestures, synth, pace, score, the renderer, the
   director's rules, reveal or the stage; do not edit the schema"
  "Do not run `bb e2e` or `bb play`"]
 :context ["docs/product/score.md" "src/halfahead/schema.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/lab/marks.cljc" "src/halfahead/lab/style.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/lab/reading.cljc" "src/halfahead/lab/pose.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/lab/director.cljc" "src/halfahead/lab/main.cljs"
           "src/halfahead/lab/debug.cljc" "public/lab/index.html"
           "e2e/lab.mjs" "docs/LAB.md" "DESIGN.md"]
 :budget-usd 12.0}
